message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived version used in your work."
type: software
title: "WSC hydrometric tools"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Hongren
    affiliation: University of Waterloo
repository-code: "https://github.com/hongren-shen/wsc-hydrometric-tools"
url: "https://github.com/hongren-shen/wsc-hydrometric-tools"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Python workflows for processing daily HYDAT observations, downloading Water
  Survey of Canada (WSC) unit-value data, and calculating hourly means for a
  single station. The tools support discharge and water level, retain source
  quality metadata in CSV outputs, and export observation time series in
  Raven RVT format. Daily cross-checks against HYDAT screen suspect Grade
  10/20 and approval-level records. Editable examples use station 02GB001,
  Grand River at Brantford, Ontario.
keywords:
  - Water Survey of Canada
  - HYDAT
  - hydrometric data
  - streamflow
  - water level
  - Raven
